{"title":"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/3/a83fd9e8408d0ef4eedc712264ee2fd9228fef07.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(u_{n})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"35\" height=\"20\" /> is defined by\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c4212437dcf3b39e8d32606195544c94d43618c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u_{0} = 2 \\quad u_{1} = \\frac {5}{2}, u_{n + 1} = u_{n}(u_{n - 1}^{2} - 2) - u_{1} \\ \\text{ for } n = 1,\\cdots\\]\" width=\"441\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Prove that for any positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> we have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/c/84c80cbc75bf044a90cc4ab9e30678b82fd5b905.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\lfloor u_{n} \\rfloor = 2^{\\frac {(2^{n} - ( - 1)^{n})}{3}}\\]\" width=\"131\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>(where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/1/441416e660d25335f27e55334ac2a06e51541c97.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\lfloor x\\rfloor$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"23\" height=\"19\" /> denotes the smallest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/3/163b0f326b6f8a5fa311f179ad175849b828e468.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\leq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"14\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />)<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/2/d52dd46b7fc4df2f724b5af4311a675147cd6e8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$.$\" width=\"3\" height=\"2\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/b/2ebf118a6d6fe7d73de0491aa14468276a9fe51a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x_n)_{n \\geq 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> be defined as \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/8/d288b0e675fb955502cb1eb97e8bb96950c9d054.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_{0}=0,x_{1}=1, x_{n}=x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}\\]\" width=\"264\" height=\"16\" />\nWe notice\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/6/1d6fc626b399715acd19b9bd6377390e295267e4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x_n=\\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}\\]\" width=\"132\" height=\"38\" />\nBecause the roots of the characteristic polynomial <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/9/88948438a1bd5d930e6b15ba0bca6cba56b6155b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{n}=x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"146\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/e/bae5aba07d37ff6ff813107e76260fb31ad5794e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"25\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>We also see <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/5/175461cec02bf3f5ee249126a3cd35319e923712.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^1-(-1)^1}{3}=1=x_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"161\" height=\"39\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc69fa83034f5d17af1132a7ddb2ea8fda995457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2^2-(-1)^2}{3}=1=x_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"161\" height=\"39\" />\nWe want to prove\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/2/ff2a4c42f8872e5e1c0aa6396cdfd3c446869a46.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{x_{n}-2x_{n-1}}+2^{-x_{n}+2x_{n-1}}=2^{x_1}+2^{-x_1}\\]\" width=\"280\" height=\"16\" />\nThis is done by induction \n</p><p>Base Case:\nFor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> ses det <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/4858b73631f75c7f9ad533e9d51f9f7aaa2aed38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{1-0}+2^{0-1}=2^{1}+2^{-1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"177\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Inductive step:\nAssume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/b/06b2a0cda6552d207acbabee8bf6ea299040afd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{x_{n-1}-2x_{n-2}}+2^{-x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}}=2^{x_1}+2^{-x_1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"310\" height=\"16\" />\nWe notice\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/9/9e9e5771604b41dbfb6748a9fdc40ffb51acf21f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  2^{x_{n}-2x_{n-1}}+2^{-x_{n}+2x_{n-1}} &amp;=2^{x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}-2x_{n-1}}+2^{-(x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2})+2x_{n-1}}\\\\ &amp;=2^{-x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}}+2^{x_{n-1}-2x_{n-2}}\\\\ &amp;=2^{x_1}+2^{-x_1} \\end{align*}\" width=\"511\" height=\"72\" /> \nWe then want to show\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/2/5528814bb9084f1f091c7607028006154b38be8b.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n=2^{x_n}+2^{-x_n}\\]\" width=\"124\" height=\"15\" />\nThis can be done using induction\n</p><p>Base Case\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d96ecc15129c5631ba4a2c6578e91e3d13e3baf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" />, it is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/8/a4899d1acd1f408fa9a3ef540553575fdc184d03.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_1=\\frac{5}{2}\\]\" width=\"52\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/4/41467b246c3ebab88c0819046a862e3c860a78ff.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{x_1}+2^{-x_1}=2^1+2^{-1}=2+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{5}{2}\\]\" width=\"274\" height=\"37\" /> Therefore, the base case is proved.\n</p><p>Inductive Step\n</p><p>Assume for all natural <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/7400e866ec206aeeca3f416d787b8bbeed9e1b54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k&lt;n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/d/24dcee358a4e9ab539dbb77976a102ae8f49e20e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k=2^{x_k}+2^{-x_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"122\" height=\"15\" />\\newline\nThen we have that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/0/410214a5b4e6c3a869c3b41a4312a92f200c5e52.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}  a_n &amp;=  a_{n}(a_{n-1}^{2}-2)-a_{1} \\\\   &amp;=  (2^{x_{n-1}}+2^{-x_{n-1}})((2^{x_{n-2}}+2^{-x_{n-2}})^2-2)-(2^{x_{1}}+2^{-x_{0}}) \\\\  &amp;= (2^{x_{n-1}}+2^{-x_{n-1}})((2^{x_{n-2}})^2+(2^{-x_{n-2}})^2+2*2^{x_{n-2}}*2^{-x_{n-2}}-2)-(2^{x_{1}}+2^{-x_{0}}) \\\\  &amp;=(2^{x_{n-1}}+2^{-x_{n-1}})((2^{2x_{n-2}})+(2^{-2x_{n-2}})+2*2^{x_{n-2}-x_{n-2}}-2)-(2^{x_{1}}+2^{-x_{0}}) \\\\  &amp;=(2^{x_{n-1}}+2^{-x_{n-1}})((2^{2x_{n-2}})+(2^{-2x_{n-2}})+2-2)-(2^{x_{1}}+2^{-x_{0}}) \\\\ &amp;=2^{x_{n-1}}*2^{2x_{n-2}}+2^{-x_{n-1}}2^{-2x_{n-2}}+2^{x_{n-1}}*2^{-2x_{n-2}}+2^{-x_{n-1}}*2^{2x_{n-2}}-2^{x_{1}}-2^{-x_{0}}\\\\ &amp;=2^{x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}}+2^{-(x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}})+2^{x_{n-1}-2x_{n-2}}+2^{-x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}}-2^{x_{1}}-2^{-x_{0}}\\\\ &amp;=2^{x_{n}}+2^{-x_{n}}+2^{x_{n-1}-2x_{n-2}}+2^{-x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}}-2^{x_{1}}-2^{-x_{0}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"651\" height=\"211\" />\nFrom our first induction proof we have that:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/7/37791e07ab8d9986e9a182d7c5586201255f3ee7.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{x_{n-1}-2x_{n-2}}+2^{-x_{n-1}+2x_{n-2}}=2^{x_1}+2^{-x_1}\\]\" width=\"309\" height=\"16\" />\nThen:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/f/07f5b50e8f31f252d0fdeb84dd15c989690a9d61.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_n=2^{x_n}+2^{-x_n}+2^{x_1}+2^{-x_1}-(2^{x_1}+2^{-x_1})=2^{x_n}+2^{-x_n}\\]\" width=\"451\" height=\"18\" />\nWe notice \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/c/bac228d5ae6934c7f90beb68f7b5638629485c76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left[a_n\\right]=\\left[2^{x_n}+2^{-x_n}\\right]=2^{x_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"199\" height=\"22\" />, Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6af6d11396babfc2a3fb6c56d7be49e6f1dd551.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{x_n} \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/f/a2f8b28857104c230b6af27a757bd5fd0737905b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{-x_n}&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"71\" height=\"18\" />, for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/4/0247db3d702b5ce6be98f50771750a2723cddcea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;0$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"43\" height=\"13\" />\nFinally we conclude\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/5/1c50564f2f80b3778264c784ebb1797ab5d4449d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left[a_n\\right]=2^{\\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}}\\]\" width=\"117\" height=\"25\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We note that there is a slightly easier claim that can be proved also by induction. By testing out smaller terms, one sees that \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/6524aa7151b332d6de3e41873f8c18c8d5c969d9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[u_n= 2^{\\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}} + 2^{- \\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}}\\]\" width=\"210\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/5/e/e5e67114e90e4c0f12e82962e548d38df58a5b4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=1,2,3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"78\" height=\"16\" /> (note that since we are using strong induction to prove this result this suffices as the base case).\n</p><p>Suppose that the equation above holds for all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/a/8aad1a58d92d1cf1d7cc28a276efb0b1557574b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\le n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"45\" height=\"15\" />. Then for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/3/0e3efd9b14723a92c2ae891fe27780d5f8e2b215.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"15\" />, one have\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e8719b207419944dbcd2595af430d852672836.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} u_{n+1} &amp;= u_n (u_{n-1} ^2 -2) -u_1 \\\\ &amp;= (2^{\\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}}+2^{- \\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}}) \\cdot ( (2^{\\frac{2^{n-1}-(-1)^{n-1}}{3}}+2^{- \\frac{2^{n-1}-(-1)^{n-1}}{3}} )^2 -2) - \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ &amp;= (2^{\\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}}+2^{- \\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}}) \\cdot ( (2^{\\frac{2^{n-1}-(-1)^{n-1}}{3}})^2 + (2^{- \\frac{2^{n-1}-(-1)^{n-1}}{3}})^2 )- \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ &amp;= (2^{\\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}}+2^{- \\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}}) \\cdot (2^{\\frac{2^{n}-2 \\cdot (-1)^{n-1}}{3}} + 2^{- \\frac{2^{n}-2 \\cdot (-1)^{n-1}}{3}})- \\frac{5}{2} \\\\ &amp;= 2^{\\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3} + \\frac{2^{n}-2 \\cdot (-1)^{n-1}}{3}} + 2^{- \\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3} - \\frac{2^{n}-2 \\cdot (-1)^{n-1}}{3}} + 2^{(-1)^n} + 2^{-(-1)^n} -\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ &amp;= 2^{\\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3} + \\frac{2^{n}-2 \\cdot (-1)^{n-1}}{3}} + 2^{- \\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3} - \\frac{2^{n}-2 \\cdot (-1)^{n-1}}{3}} \\\\ &amp;= 2^{\\frac{2^{n+1}-(-1)^{n+1}}{3}}+2^{- \\frac{2^{n+1}-(-1)^{n+1}}{3}} \\end{align*}\" width=\"595\" height=\"259\" />\n</p><p>as desired. The strong induction proves our claim. Now, it is rather obvious that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/b/24bc4e52338f3683205a3cab75c7e011651dd96d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{- \\frac{2^n-(-1)^n}{3}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"81\" height=\"22\" /> is between 0 and 1, so indeed our claim proves the result. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/c/b6cf65b1f2fbdf388e3daeff9b96b34d3399d777.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p>~<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Ddk001\" title=\"Ddk001\">Ddk001</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO\" title=\"1976 IMO\">1976 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1976_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1976 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Final Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016215630\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.027 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.045 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 246/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 867/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 52/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9823/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.848      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    6.848      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:6417:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016215630 and revision id 249335. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}